					<description><![CDATA[<img width="800" height="418" src="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Kalshi-founders" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders.jpg 800w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-300x157.jpg 300w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-768x401.jpg 768w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-380x199.jpg 380w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-760x397.jpg 760w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-600x314.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" />Kalshi, the first federally regulated U.S. prediction market exchange, reached a $40 billion valuation after a $1bn Series&#8230;]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<img width="800" height="418" src="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Kalshi-founders" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders.jpg 800w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-300x157.jpg 300w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-768x401.jpg 768w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-380x199.jpg 380w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-760x397.jpg 760w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Kalshi-founders-600x314.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" />
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Sequoia Capital and Wellington Management co-led a funding round that raised $ 1 billion at a $40 billion valuation.</li>



<li>The $40 billion valuation is roughly 10x Kalshi&#8217;s reported annualised revenue of $4 billion.</li>



<li>Kalshi plans to use the funds for leveraged event contracts, perpetual futures on individual stocks, markets based on compute prices, and its institutional business. </li>
</ul>



<p><a href="https://kalshi.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">Kalshi</a>, the first federally regulated U.S. prediction market exchange, reached a $40 billion valuation after a $1bn Series G round co-led by <a href="https://techfundingnews.com/sequoia-7b-expansion-fund-late-stage-ai/" data-type="post" data-id="64884" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sequoia Capital</a> and Wellington Management, an 82% increase from the <a href="https://techfundingnews.com/kalshi-doubles-valuation-to-22b-with-1b-raise-as-coatue-bets-on-prediction-markets/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">$22 billion valuation in May</a>.</p>



<p>Baillie Gifford, Morgan Stanley Investment Management, Coatue Management and Andreessen Horowitz all joined the round. Reuters <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/tiger-global-dragoneer-talks-invest-in-kalshis-new-1-billion-fundraise-sources-2026-09-29/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">also reported</a> that Tiger Global and Dragoneer participated. </p>]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
