					<description><![CDATA[<img width="800" height="418" src="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave.png" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Jignesh Dave, co-founder of Braid" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave.png 800w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-300x157.png 300w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-768x401.png 768w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-380x199.png 380w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-760x397.png 760w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-600x314.png 600w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" />The wholesale arm of a mobile operator turned down Jignesh Dave for nine days running. It took him&#8230;]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<img width="800" height="418" src="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave.png" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Jignesh Dave, co-founder of Braid" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave.png 800w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-300x157.png 300w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-768x401.png 768w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-380x199.png 380w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-760x397.png 760w, https://techfundingnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Jignesh-Dave-co-founder-of-Dave-600x314.png 600w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" />
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Braid, formerly Next Communications, has closed a $38 million Series A round led by Octopus Ventures, with KPN Ventures also investing.</li>



<li>The company says it&#8217;s profitable and that this is its first time raising money from outside investors.</li>



<li>Braid&#8217;s API connects to over 600 carriers in over 200 countries and is used by nearly 90 enterprise customers.</li>
</ul>



<p>The wholesale arm of a mobile operator turned down <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jigsdave/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">Jignesh Dave</a> for nine days running. It took him 18 months and half a million euros to sell his very first branded SIM card. </p>



<p>Braid, formerly Next Communications, has now raised a $38 million Series A, led by <a href="https://techfundingnews.com/octopus-ventures-wants-to-back-early-stage-startups-launches-10m-fund/" data-type="post" data-id="10318" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Octopus Ventures</a>, with KPN Ventures also on board. The Hague-based startup claims it&#8217;s profitable and has positive cash flow. </p>



<p>The funding will fund international expansion, carrier network growth, and infrastructure build-out to further cement its position in the embedded connectivity space.</p>]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
